#
# winoracle (WARP, FL 11_0), x64 and x86 identical. Vitreo differs on one line
# by choice: "[map] dynamic texture DISCARD" reports the subresource's real
# RowPitch/DepthPitch (0x10/0x40, what the immediate context reports) where
# WARP's deferred Map reports 0/0. A texture written with a 0 row pitch keeps
# only its first row, so no application can depend on it; for buffers the 0/0
# is matched. Open: a hardware (non-WARP) oracle for the texture pitch.
